-No!


00:07:02.192 --> 00:07:03.692
I can't breathe!


00:07:03.942 --> 00:07:06.400
We're going to light you on fire.
Hold still.


00:07:06.483 --> 00:07:09.025
We're lighting you on fire, hold still.


00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.900
No!


00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:13.233
Son of a bitch!


00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.233
Shut up.


00:07:14.608 --> 00:07:17.358
Hold still. Hold still right there.


00:07:52.025 --> 00:07:53.067
On your feet!


00:07:53.608 --> 00:07:54.983
Stand against the wall.


00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:56.733
Stand still.


00:07:58.192 --> 00:08:00.650
Facing the wall without touching it.


00:08:28.525 --> 00:08:29.775
Don't move.


00:08:29.858 --> 00:08:31.567
Hold still.


00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.150
Hold still, don't look at me.
Face the wall.


00:08:34.358 --> 00:08:36.275
Hold still.


00:09:11.275 --> 00:09:15.275
ABANDON ALL HOPE,
YOU WHO ENTER HERE.


00:09:21.358 --> 00:09:23.025
Here, little shit.


00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:36.233
MINISTRY OF DEFENSE
RESOLUTION


00:09:39.442 --> 00:09:43.900
YOU CANNOT SPEAK.
NOT TO EACH OTHER OR TO ANYONE.


00:09:46.442 --> 00:09:49.108
THE SOLDIERS ARE FORBIDDEN
TO TALK TO YOU.


00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:01.900
One, two, three, four.


00:10:02.233 --> 00:10:04.775
One, two, three,


00:10:04.942 --> 00:10:05.817
four.


00:10:05.983 --> 00:10:07.942
One, two, three,


00:10:08.108 --> 00:10:09.483
four.


00:10:11.108 --> 00:10:14.233
One, two, three, four.


00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.442
Stop, stop, stop.


00:10:36.525 --> 00:10:38.067
Right there.


00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:42.192
What does he think he is?
A gymnast?


00:10:42.275 --> 00:10:44.483
He could use a kick in the kidneys.


00:10:44.567 --> 00:10:45.858
A gymnasticist!


00:10:45.942 --> 00:10:47.858
You stay still. Understood?


00:11:08.025 --> 00:11:13.400
12 MONTHS LATER


00:12:49.233 --> 00:12:51.358
<i>These guys can't talk to anyone.</i>


00:12:52.025 --> 00:12:53.733
<i>Nobody can talk to them.</i>


00:12:53.983 --> 00:12:56.442
<i>Remember that they're seditious</i>
<i>and subversive.</i>


00:12:56.608 --> 00:12:58.192
<i>Traitors to our country.</i>


00:12:58.692 --> 00:13:00.067
<i>They're very dangerous.</i>


00:13:00.108 --> 00:13:02.358
<i>They can be incredibly convincing.</i>


00:13:03.108 --> 00:13:05.608
<i>Contact with them must be minimum.</i>


00:13:05.692 --> 00:13:08.608
<i>We're the National Army.</i>


00:13:08.775 --> 00:13:11.108
<i>It took us years to win this war.</i>


00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:15.192
<i>And remember that humanity</i>
<i>was always saved</i>


00:13:15.275 --> 00:13:16.525
<i>at the last minute</i>


00:13:16.608 --> 00:13:18.983
<i>by a firing squad.</i>


00:13:35.817 --> 00:13:37.400
My dear Ruso,


00:13:40.108 --> 00:13:42.400
I'm here because your family
is pestering us.


00:13:43.192 --> 00:13:44.400
I'll let you see them,


00:13:44.483 --> 00:13:46.733
but don't make things harder,


00:13:46.817 --> 00:13:49.192
because you'll make it harder
for them, and for you.


00:13:49.817 --> 00:13:52.067
And you love your family a lot, right?


00:13:55.108 --> 00:13:56.233
You know what this is?


00:13:58.692 --> 00:14:01.150
It's a resolution from
Army Central Command.


00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.358
If any attack happens,
we'll have to kill you.


00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.275
And you know that's easy.


00:14:09.067 --> 00:14:10.900
You're not prisoners anymore.


00:14:11.858 --> 00:14:13.442
You're hostages.


00:14:15.108 --> 00:14:17.442
We should have killed you
when we could.


00:14:19.025 --> 00:14:21.400
Now we're going to drive you crazy.


00:14:23.775 --> 00:14:25.817
You lost the war, Pepe.


00:14:27.108 --> 00:14:28.900
<i>Now you are doomed.</i>


00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:33.775
And you wanted to change the world?


00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.983
Just look at yourselves.


00:14:40.817 --> 00:14:42.150
<i>I would kill myself.</i>


00:14:42.358 --> 00:14:44.442
<i>Why don't you kill yourselves?</i>


00:14:50.817 --> 00:14:51.692
Stay still.


00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:54.400
I said stay still.


00:15:12.608 --> 00:15:15.192
Look, this is barbaric.


00:15:16.108 --> 00:15:19.483
A firing squad
would be more humane.


00:15:31.192 --> 00:15:32.692
Rosencof, get ready.


00:15:47.275 --> 00:15:48.483
Dad.


00:15:49.358 --> 00:15:50.775
Hi!


00:15:51.567 --> 00:15:53.275
How are you, sweetheart?


00:15:55.692 --> 00:15:57.483
What beautiful eyes you have.


00:15:58.942 --> 00:16:00.483
And school?


00:16:00.608 --> 00:16:01.858
How are things at school?


00:16:02.025 --> 00:16:04.317
-We brought you food.
-Thanks, Mom.


00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.525
-And notebooks and books...
-Thanks, Mom.


00:16:06.692 --> 00:16:08.525
-How are you, darling?
-Fine.


00:16:08.608 --> 00:16:10.192
You're so big!


00:16:13.108 --> 00:16:14.567
What a lovely surprise.


00:16:16.067 --> 00:16:18.192
What do you do here every day?


00:16:20.275 --> 00:16:21.817
We walk.


00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:23.817
You have recess?


00:16:26.108 --> 00:16:27.650
Yeah, sure.


00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:32.275
We brought Alejandrita's
new glasses to show you.


00:16:32.983 --> 00:16:34.192
Put them on.


00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:36.733
Wait, wait.
Tell him to close his eyes.


00:16:36.942 --> 00:16:38.692
Close your eyes.


00:16:40.108 --> 00:16:41.567
I'm closing them.


00:16:42.525 --> 00:16:43.650
They're closed.


00:16:54.108 --> 00:16:56.025
-Can I open them?
-Yes.


00:17:05.817 --> 00:17:07.608
They look beautiful on you.


00:17:07.775 --> 00:17:12.150
Oh, Dad. These glasses make me cry.


00:17:13.358 --> 00:17:15.442
No, sweetie. Don't use them
if they make you cry.


00:17:16.442 --> 00:17:17.567
They make her cry?


00:17:18.567 --> 00:17:20.025
The lenses make her cry.


00:17:26.858 --> 00:17:27.900
Isaac...


00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:32.025
Hey, Dad. Are you okay?


00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.275
What's wrong?


00:17:33.858 --> 00:17:36.150
-Who is he?
-Mauricio.


00:17:37.067 --> 00:17:38.108
I came to see my son.


00:17:38.192 --> 00:17:40.733
-Isaac, please.
-Dad, it's me.


00:17:40.817 --> 00:17:42.900
-Where is my son?
-Calm down.


00:17:42.983 --> 00:17:45.108
-Isaac, sit down.
-Where is my son?


00:17:45.358 --> 00:17:47.942
-I came to see my son.
-Sit down.


00:17:48.108 --> 00:17:52.150
-Dad, it's me.
-No, please, sit down.


00:17:52.358 --> 00:17:53.192
Sit down.


00:17:53.275 --> 00:17:54.275
No!


00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:55.275
Isaac!


00:17:55.358 --> 00:17:56.983
Dad, are you okay?


00:17:57.733 --> 00:17:59.400
Dad!


00:17:59.567 --> 00:18:01.150
Don't move!


00:18:02.108 --> 00:18:03.192
Dad!


00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.525
-Isaac, no!
-Dad!


00:18:13.275 --> 00:18:14.858
Dad, it's me!


00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:18.650
Dad, it's me!


00:18:29.025 --> 00:18:30.858
Let's go!


00:18:32.025 --> 00:18:33.275
Come on!


00:18:38.108 --> 00:18:42.192
803 DAYS


00:19:31.108 --> 00:19:32.775
Be careful!


00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.108
Quiet, little shit!


00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:51.983
Get out of there! Out!


00:21:01.983 --> 00:21:03.150
Merry Christmas!


00:23:57.483 --> 00:23:59.025
A, b, c...


00:23:59.150 --> 00:24:01.775
A, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i,...


00:24:04.608 --> 00:24:06.067
D, e, f, g,...


00:24:30.233 --> 00:24:32.608
Merry Christmas, Ruso.


00:24:33.150 --> 00:24:36.108
Merry Christmas to you too, Ñato.


00:24:45.025 --> 00:24:49.108
1074 DAYS


00:25:01.192 --> 00:25:03.900
<i>Are we in Solis?</i>


00:25:04.067 --> 00:25:05.608
<i>I don't know.</i>


00:25:17.108 --> 00:25:19.025
<i>In 5th Cavalry.</i>


00:25:20.233 --> 00:25:22.358
<i>How do you know?</i>


00:25:22.525 --> 00:25:25.525
<i>By their boots.</i>


00:25:26.900 --> 00:25:30.692
<i>Where is Pepe?</i>


00:25:31.358 --> 00:25:32.567
<i>No idea.</i>


00:26:01.025 --> 00:26:03.025
<i>Checkmate.</i>


00:26:03.442 --> 00:26:06.025
<i>Checkmate how?</i>


00:26:07.358 --> 00:26:10.775
<i>With queen on D4.</i>


00:26:15.108 --> 00:26:15.942
You're shitting me.


00:26:16.817 --> 00:26:19.192
<i>Queen D4 I win.</i>


00:26:20.983 --> 00:26:24.358
<i>Arguing with you...</i>


00:26:24.858 --> 00:26:28.108
<i>is like talking to a wall.</i>


00:26:48.650 --> 00:26:50.817
Hurry up. Crap quickly.


00:26:57.400 --> 00:26:58.858
I can't like this.


00:26:59.025 --> 00:27:00.858
I can't squat, I can't shit.


00:27:01.150 --> 00:27:02.275
What do you want me to do?


00:27:02.358 --> 00:27:04.233
Loosen it a little bit for me.


00:27:04.442 --> 00:27:06.108
I'm not authorized.


00:27:06.275 --> 00:27:08.650
So I'll have to shit all over the place...


00:27:10.317 --> 00:27:12.108
Corporal, there's a problem.


00:27:12.692 --> 00:27:15.067
<i>He can't reach the toilet.</i>
<i>He can't defecate.</i>


00:27:16.858 --> 00:27:17.942
Show me.


00:27:19.942 --> 00:27:21.192
I can't bend over.


00:27:22.358 --> 00:27:24.817
-Gutiérrez, type it.
-Sergeant, sir.


00:27:24.942 --> 00:27:26.525
The prisoner is tied...


00:27:31.650 --> 00:27:32.900
Faster, faster!


00:27:33.108 --> 00:27:34.858
<i>In the neighborhood...</i>


00:27:35.150 --> 00:27:36.817
-Sergeant, sir.
-What is it?


00:28:00.733 --> 00:28:02.150
-Sergeant!
-Attention!


00:28:02.233 --> 00:28:04.275
-Lieutenant!
-What's going on?


00:28:04.442 --> 00:28:07.108
<i>A complicated circumstance.</i>


00:28:08.233 --> 00:28:10.817
You see, Lieutenant?
This is the situation we have.


00:28:11.108 --> 00:28:14.358
You call me for this?
You can't solve this yourself?


00:28:14.442 --> 00:28:16.692
Captain, we have a problem
in the bathroom.


00:28:16.858 --> 00:28:18.108
Is it clogged?


00:28:22.692 --> 00:28:24.692
You really need to take a crap?


00:28:28.775 --> 00:28:30.275
Major, sir.


00:28:31.608 --> 00:28:33.025
Attention!


00:28:39.192 --> 00:28:41.192
Are you all retards?


00:28:55.067 --> 00:28:56.733
Can somebody come in here?


00:29:03.025 --> 00:29:03.858
Guard!


00:29:11.733 --> 00:29:13.608
<i>Televisions 1200.</i>


00:29:15.192 --> 00:29:17.025
<i>What a robbery!</i>


00:29:21.650 --> 00:29:24.067
<i>Pompidou dead.</i>


00:29:28.067 --> 00:29:30.983
<i>Abba won Eurovision.</i>


00:29:32.233 --> 00:29:33.692
<i>Abba what?</i>


00:29:34.275 --> 00:29:38.858
<i>Swiss music group.</i>


00:29:48.733 --> 00:29:50.817
<i>Lose consciousness...</i>


00:29:53.942 --> 00:29:56.150
<i>Need to be precise...</i>


00:30:15.817 --> 00:30:18.525
Stop thinking!
It's impossible to stop thinking!


00:30:22.567 --> 00:30:26.192
<i>Stop. Stop.</i>


00:30:27.942 --> 00:30:29.942
<i>Shut up!</i>


00:30:47.733 --> 00:30:48.983
<i>Son.</i>


00:30:49.942 --> 00:30:50.900
<i>Son.</i>


00:30:51.067 --> 00:30:52.442
Mom.


00:31:23.817 --> 00:31:26.817
VICTORY OR DEATH


00:31:28.567 --> 00:31:30.400
-Good afternoon.
-Afternoon.


00:31:30.567 --> 00:31:31.525
I'm here to see my son.


00:31:31.650 --> 00:31:33.525
-Who?
-José Mujica.


00:31:33.608 --> 00:31:36.025
The courthouse said he might be here.


00:31:36.150 --> 00:31:37.608
Your ID.


00:31:39.275 --> 00:31:41.192
Sign this and wait here.


00:31:46.525 --> 00:31:49.525
<i>I brought you mate</i>
<i>and dulce de leche.</i>


00:31:49.733 --> 00:31:51.525
<i>The shirt you like.</i>


00:31:51.775 --> 00:31:53.358
How's the neighborhood?


00:31:53.567 --> 00:31:56.275
<i>The neighborhood is fine.</i>


00:31:56.483 --> 00:31:57.983
And Grandpa?


00:31:58.067 --> 00:32:00.150
<i>Grandpa misses you.</i>


00:32:03.108 --> 00:32:04.150
Ma'am!


00:32:04.858 --> 00:32:07.400
They're checking documentation!


00:32:07.817 --> 00:32:09.525
Why don't you wait inside?


00:32:09.900 --> 00:32:12.233
No, I'm fine right here.


00:32:18.442 --> 00:32:19.567
Mom.


00:32:19.733 --> 00:32:21.275
Stop coming.


00:32:21.942 --> 00:32:24.400
<i>As long as I'm alive, I'll come.</i>


00:32:24.733 --> 00:32:26.483
<i>Even if I have to crawl.</i>


00:32:30.025 --> 00:32:31.233
Ma'am!


00:32:35.983 --> 00:32:38.775
I'm sorry, but your son isn't available.


00:32:39.567 --> 00:32:40.983
He isn't here?


00:32:41.108 --> 00:32:43.358
I don't have that information.


00:32:43.733 --> 00:32:45.275
Where is he?


00:32:45.483 --> 00:32:47.608
I don't have that information.


00:32:48.358 --> 00:32:50.692
What information do you have?


00:32:50.858 --> 00:32:52.608
The information I gave you.


00:32:53.233 --> 00:32:56.067
But what information did you give me?


00:32:56.192 --> 00:32:58.233
I don't have that information.


00:33:10.858 --> 00:33:12.400
Mom, come here!


00:33:14.775 --> 00:33:16.192
Come back!


00:33:19.150 --> 00:33:20.192
Mom...


00:34:51.192 --> 00:34:52.567
That's it.


00:35:22.983 --> 00:35:27.692
DO NOT CROSS


00:35:28.567 --> 00:35:32.692
1529 DAYS


00:35:33.608 --> 00:35:38.067
I knew her because she was
Ñango's ex-girlfriend.


00:35:38.192 --> 00:35:40.275
And I always liked her.


00:35:40.483 --> 00:35:43.150
We started dancing
and I got closer to her.


00:35:43.358 --> 00:35:45.525
She smelled like soap.


00:35:45.692 --> 00:35:47.983
So clean.


00:35:48.108 --> 00:35:51.442
I hadn't been around that in a long time.


00:35:51.608 --> 00:35:55.192
-Brunette?
-Yeah.


00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:59.233
We danced to like two songs
and she said come tomorrow.


00:35:59.442 --> 00:36:02.942
I put on cologne, a nice shirt...


00:36:03.317 --> 00:36:06.442
When I went, she wasn't there.
I don't know if she stood me up.


00:36:06.525 --> 00:36:08.442
I should have got answered.


00:36:08.858 --> 00:36:11.317
I left her flowers, chocolates...


00:36:11.400 --> 00:36:14.567
-Which flowers?
-The flowers were...


00:36:14.692 --> 00:36:18.192
The ones with yellow in the middle.


00:36:18.400 --> 00:36:20.400
-Daisies.
-Right, daisies.


00:36:20.567 --> 00:36:24.817
I know women, always the same.
It happened to me once.


00:36:24.942 --> 00:36:27.108
-They leave you hanging.
-What did you do?


00:36:27.275 --> 00:36:28.900
Nothing, I never saw her again.


00:36:29.025 --> 00:36:31.650
I think they were mocking me.


00:36:32.983 --> 00:36:36.858
There was something.
You know when you feel it?


00:36:36.983 --> 00:36:38.275
We made eye contact...


00:36:38.775 --> 00:36:43.275
By the third song
we were closer together...


00:36:43.483 --> 00:36:46.108
And she gave me a kiss
right here on the cheek.


00:36:46.233 --> 00:36:50.358
And I was like, "No..."


00:36:50.525 --> 00:36:52.192
Stop! Stop...


00:36:53.775 --> 00:36:55.192
Silence!


00:36:55.983 --> 00:36:57.983
Stop, Barriola, please.


00:36:58.108 --> 00:36:59.817
-Barriola?
-Stop.


00:36:59.900 --> 00:37:02.025
How do you know my name?


00:37:02.150 --> 00:37:06.567
You never stop talking! The girl,
the ex-boyfriend, the dance, the kiss...


00:37:06.733 --> 00:37:09.650
You need to move.
She's interested, but make a move.


00:37:09.817 --> 00:37:10.733
Shut your mouth!


00:37:10.817 --> 00:37:13.358
Let me think. Listen.


00:37:13.692 --> 00:37:17.358
Maybe her boyfriend is in town
and that's why she's ignoring you.


00:37:17.483 --> 00:37:20.733
How do you know?
Shut up or I'll kick your ass.


00:37:20.817 --> 00:37:22.275
Here's what we'll do.


00:37:22.483 --> 00:37:24.983
Bring me down a pen
and paper and I'll help you.


00:37:25.483 --> 00:37:27.275
-I want to help you, really.
-Shut up!


00:37:27.358 --> 00:37:30.108
You have to surprise women, Barriola.


00:37:30.525 --> 00:37:31.692
Bring me a pen and paper...


00:37:31.858 --> 00:37:33.567
I'll stick the pen up your ass!


00:37:33.692 --> 00:37:36.775
Please, Barriola, let's solve this.
I can't listen to you anymore.


00:37:36.858 --> 00:37:38.900
Stop calling me by my name!


00:37:51.358 --> 00:37:52.817
Hey, little shit.


00:37:55.442 --> 00:37:57.442
What do you want
the paper and pen for?


00:37:57.608 --> 00:37:59.817
For you to write her a letter.


00:38:00.108 --> 00:38:01.442
What for?


00:38:03.150 --> 00:38:06.692
Because you said she was hot,
I thought you liked her.


00:38:09.275 --> 00:38:10.525
You dictate,


00:38:10.608 --> 00:38:12.108
I'll write it down.


00:38:12.275 --> 00:38:13.275
But I'm warning you,


00:38:13.358 --> 00:38:16.775
if you're pulling my leg,
I'll kick your ass.


00:38:20.608 --> 00:38:24.775
"And here, in the infinite solitude
of guard duty,


00:38:27.983 --> 00:38:30.108
imprisoned by your absence..."


00:38:30.150 --> 00:38:32.150
Slow down, slow down.


00:38:33.692 --> 00:38:36.150
"Imprisoned by your absence,


00:38:37.983 --> 00:38:43.025
I can feel my tear ducts


00:38:43.483 --> 00:38:45.108
quivering."


00:38:50.775 --> 00:38:53.025
And? What now?


00:38:53.358 --> 00:38:55.525
-What do you mean?
-What do I do?


00:38:56.650 --> 00:38:58.525
You send it to her, soldier!


00:39:09.733 --> 00:39:12.442
On your feet, let's go.


00:39:19.483 --> 00:39:21.067
Shitty Tupamaro.


00:39:21.192 --> 00:39:23.567
When the sergeant gets here
you'll get the club.


00:39:34.108 --> 00:39:36.067
Take off his hood, soldier.


00:39:37.733 --> 00:39:39.192
Everyone get out.


00:39:39.567 --> 00:39:41.317
Everybody out!


00:39:41.733 --> 00:39:43.108
Move it!


00:39:52.442 --> 00:39:54.400
So you're the writer.


00:39:58.275 --> 00:40:00.650
Look, I have a problem.


00:40:04.192 --> 00:40:06.400
There's a girl I like.


00:40:07.275 --> 00:40:09.525
I heard you can help me.


00:40:11.942 --> 00:40:13.108
Who is she?


00:40:14.233 --> 00:40:15.567
What's she like?


00:40:16.358 --> 00:40:17.858
She's...


00:40:18.025 --> 00:40:21.192
brunette, pretty...


00:40:21.942 --> 00:40:26.442
I met her last week.
We were playing around.


00:40:27.192 --> 00:40:30.358
I asked her out,
but she doesn't want to.


00:40:40.858 --> 00:40:42.233
What's her name?


00:40:42.817 --> 00:40:43.900
Nelly.


00:40:50.275 --> 00:40:52.942
-Brunette, you said?
-Yeah.


00:40:53.108 --> 00:40:55.358
She works with her mom in the bakery.


00:40:56.900 --> 00:40:59.358
And she makes warm bread
in the morning?


00:40:59.817 --> 00:41:01.942
Yeah, that bread with fat.


00:41:13.567 --> 00:41:14.692
Just...


00:41:15.483 --> 00:41:18.358
sign it with your name
so it looks better.


00:41:31.983 --> 00:41:33.150
Thank you.


00:41:38.358 --> 00:41:41.192
Can I keep the notebook?


00:41:45.608 --> 00:41:46.900
Please.


00:42:01.775 --> 00:42:02.983
Thank you.


00:42:03.108 --> 00:42:04.442
Soldiers!


00:42:06.525 --> 00:42:08.108
Take him away.


00:42:35.567 --> 00:42:37.567
I brought hot bread.


00:42:38.650 --> 00:42:39.567
Thank you.


00:42:44.733 --> 00:42:46.358
We went out last night.


00:42:48.400 --> 00:42:51.358
But the girl is very confused,
she has a lot of doubts.


00:42:51.442 --> 00:42:54.483
What doubts, if I may ask?


00:42:54.650 --> 00:42:56.108
I...


00:42:57.567 --> 00:42:59.900
got married very young.


00:43:01.192 --> 00:43:03.067
I was still in the militia


00:43:03.192 --> 00:43:05.358
and I met another girl.


00:43:06.733 --> 00:43:09.525
When I went back home,
I was a different man.


00:43:10.025 --> 00:43:11.692
I had changed a lot.


00:43:12.483 --> 00:43:16.608
I have a daughter from that marriage.


00:43:17.442 --> 00:43:19.275
She's all grown up.


00:43:19.483 --> 00:43:20.942
She doesn't talk to me.


00:43:21.775 --> 00:43:23.192
That hurts.


00:43:26.817 --> 00:43:30.608
And now that I want
to make a new life for myself,


00:43:31.108 --> 00:43:34.733
it's like a pebble in my shoe.


00:43:35.858 --> 00:43:36.942
Sergeant,


00:43:39.817 --> 00:43:41.900
we all make mistakes.


00:44:18.400 --> 00:44:19.400
Goal!


00:44:20.775 --> 00:44:21.858
Goal!


00:44:26.733 --> 00:44:28.025
Help me.


00:44:29.025 --> 00:44:30.650
How do I answer?


00:44:34.233 --> 00:44:36.483
What are you looking for with her?


00:44:37.108 --> 00:44:39.067
I don't know, I'm older now.


00:44:39.192 --> 00:44:42.108
I don't want to end my life alone,
I want to end it with her.


00:44:43.108 --> 00:44:44.442
Should I write that?


00:44:46.150 --> 00:44:47.942
You're the writer.


00:44:49.650 --> 00:44:51.025
What would you do?


00:44:51.858 --> 00:44:53.650
I wouldn't tell her yet.


00:44:54.775 --> 00:44:56.858
We need to make her fall in love first.


00:45:12.608 --> 00:45:13.567
Yes.


00:45:29.733 --> 00:45:31.108
Of you.


00:45:31.733 --> 00:45:33.067
<i>Of me.</i>


00:45:33.692 --> 00:45:34.858
<i>Of the air.</i>


00:45:36.983 --> 00:45:38.692
<i>Of the shadow of before.</i>


00:45:38.775 --> 00:45:39.942
<i>Of after.</i>


00:45:43.775 --> 00:45:45.275
<i>Of who knows love.</i>


00:45:50.983 --> 00:45:53.442
<i>Give me back the Word.</i>


00:45:55.775 --> 00:45:57.733
Keep pedalling, I'm letting go.


00:46:01.567 --> 00:46:02.567
Good, sweetie!


00:46:04.525 --> 00:46:05.567
Keep going!


00:46:07.608 --> 00:46:09.692
Good! You're on your own!


00:46:09.858 --> 00:46:11.442
Look at me, Daddy!


00:46:55.900 --> 00:46:57.358
Raise my hood.


00:46:57.525 --> 00:46:59.900
Please, only for a second.


00:47:33.567 --> 00:47:37.692
2024 DAYS


00:47:47.567 --> 00:47:50.192
Let's go, hurry up!


00:47:55.858 --> 00:47:58.358
Keep moving, let's go.


00:48:10.983 --> 00:48:12.275
Where the fuck are we?


00:48:20.775 --> 00:48:22.525
Please, where are we?


00:48:25.442 --> 00:48:26.817
Where are we?


00:48:27.817 --> 00:48:29.358
Open up!


00:48:29.525 --> 00:48:30.942
Let us out of here!


00:49:00.900 --> 00:49:02.108
<i>Don't play dumb, Mujica.</i>


00:49:02.275 --> 00:49:04.442
<i>Tell me about...</i>


00:49:05.400 --> 00:49:06.900
<i>your contacts.</i>


00:49:07.067 --> 00:49:10.567
<i>I'm not going to think,</i>
<i>I'm not going to think...</i>


00:49:10.775 --> 00:49:13.067
<i>You must have contacts...</i>


00:49:14.567 --> 00:49:18.608
I'm not going to think!
I'm not going to think!


00:49:18.775 --> 00:49:20.400
You won't get shit out of me!


00:49:20.483 --> 00:49:22.192
I'm not going to think!


00:49:22.275 --> 00:49:23.483
<i>What are your next movements?</i>


00:49:23.567 --> 00:49:24.817
What are you saying?


00:49:27.608 --> 00:49:31.025
Speak clearly!
What are you saying? Speak clearly!


00:49:31.150 --> 00:49:34.317
Tell me what you want!
Are you on my left or right?


00:49:34.400 --> 00:49:35.817
What the fuck?


00:49:35.983 --> 00:49:37.108
What are you saying?


00:49:37.150 --> 00:49:38.983
What? Go ahead, talk!


00:49:40.025 --> 00:49:40.983
Speak!


00:49:41.108 --> 00:49:42.108
Go ahead!


00:49:42.275 --> 00:49:43.775
I'm not going to think in my head!


00:49:43.942 --> 00:49:45.983
You won't get shit out of me!


00:49:46.108 --> 00:49:47.942
I'm not going to think!


00:49:50.608 --> 00:49:52.108
Let him out!


00:49:52.608 --> 00:49:55.108
Let us out of here!


00:49:55.233 --> 00:49:56.858
Let him out!


00:49:57.275 --> 00:49:58.400
Pepe!


00:49:58.900 --> 00:50:00.942
Let us out!


00:50:03.400 --> 00:50:06.692
Come here if you're a man!
Come here!


00:51:10.608 --> 00:51:11.942
Hi, Ñato.


00:51:31.692 --> 00:51:32.900
Ñato.


00:51:37.775 --> 00:51:39.900
<i>There's someone I want you to meet.</i>


00:51:42.525 --> 00:51:44.108
<i>She was born in the barracks</i>


00:51:44.192 --> 00:51:47.358
<i>and she wants to meet you, Ñato.</i>
<i>She wants to meet you.</i>


00:51:50.067 --> 00:51:51.358
<i>Gabrielita.</i>


00:51:55.525 --> 00:51:57.608
<i>Gabrielita wants to meet you,</i>


00:51:57.775 --> 00:51:59.108
<i>but it's not easy.</i>


00:52:04.108 --> 00:52:06.150
<i>They're constantly moving you.</i>


00:52:07.233 --> 00:52:11.108
You're in Melo now,
and I'm in Punta Rieles.


00:52:11.358 --> 00:52:13.525
I don't want her to see me like this.


00:52:13.858 --> 00:52:15.858
She'll think her father is living dead.


00:52:15.942 --> 00:52:17.275
Ñato...


00:52:20.442 --> 00:52:22.150
She'll think she has no father.


00:52:32.567 --> 00:52:33.525
<i>Ñato...</i>


00:52:36.025 --> 00:52:37.942
<i>This will be over soon.</i>


00:52:42.067 --> 00:52:43.233
<i>What do we do?</i>


00:53:57.067 --> 00:53:59.275
<i>No, Sir. No, Sir.</i>


00:54:31.942 --> 00:54:33.275
<i>Tell me, Mujica.</i>


00:54:33.358 --> 00:54:35.358
<i>Who are your contacts here?</i>


00:54:36.608 --> 00:54:38.067
<i>What do you know about Ortega?</i>


00:54:39.733 --> 00:54:41.358
What is it you propose?


00:54:41.483 --> 00:54:42.650
<i>Tell me about...</i>


00:54:42.817 --> 00:54:44.567
<i>the Nicaraguan revolution.</i>


00:54:44.733 --> 00:54:48.483
<i>Communists are all the same,</i>
<i>none of you know anything.</i>


00:54:48.650 --> 00:54:51.108
<i>Only when it suits you.</i>


00:54:51.233 --> 00:54:53.858
Do you agree yes, or do you agree no?


00:55:09.358 --> 00:55:10.567
Another round?


00:55:11.400 --> 00:55:13.900
We have to figure out
how we'll get the tools.


00:55:14.067 --> 00:55:16.608
We have to try them out.


00:55:17.108 --> 00:55:17.983
And the noise.


00:55:18.108 --> 00:55:19.692
We have to try them out
and do noise tests.


00:55:19.858 --> 00:55:21.608
She said it would be fine.


00:55:21.775 --> 00:55:23.192
The basement?


00:55:23.358 --> 00:55:25.817
-The basement is perfect.
-Can you hear outside?


00:55:25.900 --> 00:55:28.233
You can't hear anything. It's huge.


00:55:29.400 --> 00:55:30.317
Thank you.


00:55:32.150 --> 00:55:33.983
Add two people to the middle column.


00:55:34.067 --> 00:55:35.942
-That's where people will come.
-Try them out.


00:55:36.858 --> 00:55:38.483
How are we going to do it?


00:55:38.817 --> 00:55:40.233
The casino is open


00:55:41.067 --> 00:55:43.108
from 8 to 5. Only during carnival.


00:55:43.150 --> 00:55:45.983
-How many will participate?
-Fifteen.


00:55:46.108 --> 00:55:47.983
-Fifteen?
-Fifteen maximum.


00:55:48.108 --> 00:55:49.192
That's a lot.


00:55:49.400 --> 00:55:52.483
<i>The Tupamaros have pulled off what people</i>
<i>are calling the heist of the century</i>


00:55:52.650 --> 00:55:56.275
<i>against the multi-million-dollar</i>
<i>tobacco company Maihlos.</i>


00:55:56.442 --> 00:55:59.900
<i>Thanks to documents</i>
<i>revealed by the Tupamaros</i>


00:56:00.067 --> 00:56:02.025
<i>the judge ordered a prison sentence</i>


00:56:02.150 --> 00:56:03.983
<i>for Narciso Eduardo Maihlos</i>


00:56:04.108 --> 00:56:07.733
<i>for tax fraud and contraband.</i>


00:56:25.358 --> 00:56:26.358
Are you okay?


00:56:27.067 --> 00:56:28.150
Yes.


00:56:28.358 --> 00:56:29.692
Another round?


00:56:33.525 --> 00:56:35.192
Do you know you're being recorded?


00:56:36.942 --> 00:56:38.150
Do you know?


00:56:39.358 --> 00:56:40.775
Anything else?


00:56:44.233 --> 00:56:45.233
Pepe.


00:56:45.483 --> 00:56:46.692
Pepe.


00:56:46.858 --> 00:56:48.400
You're being recorded.


00:56:49.025 --> 00:56:50.400
You have an antenna.


00:56:57.775 --> 00:56:58.608
<i>The basement?</i>


00:56:58.692 --> 00:57:00.733
<i>The basement is perfect.</i>


00:57:00.858 --> 00:57:02.150
<i>Can you hear outside?</i>


00:57:02.358 --> 00:57:04.525
<i>You can't hear anything. It's huge.</i>


00:57:04.692 --> 00:57:06.858
<i>-How are we going to do it?</i>
<i>-Only during carnival.</i>


00:57:15.442 --> 00:57:16.317
Stop it!


00:57:16.400 --> 00:57:18.067
Stop it!


00:57:18.108 --> 00:57:19.442
Shut up!


00:57:19.525 --> 00:57:20.775
Shut up!


00:57:23.233 --> 00:57:24.275
Another round?


00:57:59.067 --> 00:58:00.108
Sorry.


00:58:02.567 --> 00:58:04.108
I got the lyrics wrong.


00:58:12.775 --> 00:58:13.775
Mom?


00:58:34.858 --> 00:58:36.108
Identification.


00:58:39.108 --> 00:58:39.942
Sit down.


00:58:40.025 --> 00:58:41.400
Damn it, sit down!


00:58:41.567 --> 00:58:43.400
Stop, stop!


00:58:45.733 --> 00:58:47.442
Stop, Pepe!


00:59:33.025 --> 00:59:37.400
<i>In a successful operation carried out</i>
<i>by the Montevideo police,</i>


00:59:37.483 --> 00:59:43.108
<i>a rebel from a known gang of conspirers</i>
<i>was seriously wounded.</i>


00:59:44.400 --> 00:59:47.358
<i>The stranger who was carrying fake ID</i>


00:59:47.442 --> 00:59:49.775
<i>turned out to be José Alberto Mujica.</i>


00:59:49.942 --> 00:59:53.442
<i>Wanted for some time</i>
<i>as a member of the organization.</i>


00:59:54.275 --> 00:59:56.942
<i>Mujica is now being held</i>
<i>in a military hospital</i>


00:59:57.108 --> 00:59:59.108
<i>in critical condition.</i>


01:00:49.525 --> 01:00:53.067
How old are you, kid?


01:00:55.192 --> 01:00:58.567
You hadn't even been born
when they put us in here.


01:01:00.358 --> 01:01:02.233
They forgot about us.


01:01:09.025 --> 01:01:11.025
They forgot about us.


01:01:46.525 --> 01:01:50.650
2391 DAYS


01:03:01.150 --> 01:03:03.817
<i>And if this were</i>


01:03:04.275 --> 01:03:07.275
<i>my last poem,</i>


01:03:07.358 --> 01:03:09.400
<i>rebellious and sad,</i>


01:03:09.483 --> 01:03:13.192
<i>worn out but whole,</i>


01:03:13.400 --> 01:03:17.192
<i>I would only write one word:</i>


01:03:18.775 --> 01:03:22.775
<i>Companion.</i>


01:03:27.150 --> 01:03:31.067
<i>Visit tomorrow.</i>
<i>First time see Gabrielita.</i>


01:03:32.358 --> 01:03:35.150
<i>I'm scared, Ruso.</i>


01:03:35.358 --> 01:03:39.192
<i>You have a daughter.</i>
<i>What do I do?</i>


01:03:40.983 --> 01:03:43.858
<i>Tell her a story.</i>


01:03:45.692 --> 01:03:48.817
<i>I don't know any.</i>


01:03:51.358 --> 01:03:53.233
<i>Tell her this one:</i>


01:03:53.442 --> 01:03:56.692
<i>Then the little girl receives a gift:</i>


01:03:57.067 --> 01:03:59.150
A machine that makes her dreams


01:03:59.233 --> 01:04:00.150
come true.


01:04:00.692 --> 01:04:02.108
Then one day the girl


01:04:02.150 --> 01:04:04.650
was with her mother
and her mother said:


01:04:04.817 --> 01:04:07.483
"Go and feed the blue chicks."


01:04:07.650 --> 01:04:10.233
"Mom, there's no such thing
as blue chicks."


01:04:11.275 --> 01:04:12.608
"Go anyway."


01:04:13.108 --> 01:04:15.192
And when she went to feed them,


01:04:15.275 --> 01:04:19.400
she started hearing chicks
cheeping everywhere.


01:04:20.108 --> 01:04:21.025
-Cheep, cheep!
-Right.


01:04:21.150 --> 01:04:23.358
-Cheep, cheep!
-That's right.


01:04:23.525 --> 01:04:26.942
That night, when she goes to bed,
she lies down to sleep


01:04:27.233 --> 01:04:29.692
and she dreams of elephants.


01:04:29.858 --> 01:04:31.275
When she wakes up the next day,


01:04:31.483 --> 01:04:34.733
she sees elephants
walking around her house


01:04:34.900 --> 01:04:37.692
and she says,
"Look, Mom! Elephants!"


01:04:37.858 --> 01:04:39.275
Thirty seconds.


01:04:43.942 --> 01:04:48.275
Gabi, the next time you come,
I'll finish the story, okay?


01:04:49.442 --> 01:04:52.275
Daddy, why don't you have any hands?


01:04:55.067 --> 01:04:56.525
No, I do have hands.


01:04:56.692 --> 01:04:59.942
It's just that my hands
transform as well.


01:05:00.108 --> 01:05:02.400
They turn into animals, look.


01:05:03.358 --> 01:05:04.442
Look.


01:05:05.275 --> 01:05:06.858
A butterfly.


01:05:07.942 --> 01:05:09.692
What do butterflies do?


01:05:10.483 --> 01:05:11.233
That's it.


01:05:14.400 --> 01:05:15.650
A monkey.


01:05:18.525 --> 01:05:19.692
A dog.


01:05:22.692 --> 01:05:24.483
The visit is over.


01:05:28.942 --> 01:05:31.233
Bye, Gabi. I love you a lot.


01:08:03.067 --> 01:08:05.942
<i>Francisco Franco's heart</i>
<i>stopped beating...</i>


01:08:06.692 --> 01:08:08.400
<i>Caudillo of Spain...</i>


01:08:13.567 --> 01:08:16.108
<i>...after intervention by the army...</i>


01:08:16.275 --> 01:08:18.608
<i>"One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest"</i>
<i>won the Oscar</i>


01:08:18.775 --> 01:08:21.817
<i>for Best Picture and its actors,</i>


01:08:21.942 --> 01:08:24.650
<i>Jack Nicholson and Louise Fletcher</i>


01:08:24.775 --> 01:08:26.900
<i>won Best Actor and Best Actress.</i>


01:08:33.942 --> 01:08:37.567
<i>For the signing of the agreement</i>
<i>at Camp David,</i>


01:08:37.650 --> 01:08:40.150
<i>attended by the ex-President</i>
<i>of the United States,</i>


01:08:40.358 --> 01:08:42.067
<i>Jimmy Carter...</i>


01:08:42.192 --> 01:08:46.650
<i>It might hail the next few days</i>
<i>in some areas of Uruguay...</i>


01:08:55.608 --> 01:08:57.608
They have the basics, a bed,


01:08:57.692 --> 01:09:00.567
a curtain, light,
we're always attentive


01:09:00.650 --> 01:09:03.942
to requirements for general hygiene,


01:09:04.108 --> 01:09:07.608
rations or anything else
they might request,


01:09:07.775 --> 01:09:10.358
they're attended to...


01:09:35.108 --> 01:09:38.025
Say anything stupid
and we'll rip your head off.


01:09:38.483 --> 01:09:39.733
Got it?


01:09:54.442 --> 01:09:55.942
What is your name?


01:09:56.775 --> 01:09:58.275
State your name.


01:10:01.192 --> 01:10:03.608
Eleuterio Fernández Huidobro.


01:10:03.775 --> 01:10:05.108
Are you all right?


01:10:05.275 --> 01:10:06.525
The prisoner is fine.


01:10:06.692 --> 01:10:08.525
I'd like to hear it from him.


01:10:10.858 --> 01:10:12.483
INTERNATIONAL
RED CROSS COMMITTEE


01:10:18.108 --> 01:10:19.692
They barely feed us.


01:10:20.192 --> 01:10:22.483
We're not allowed to talk to each other.


01:10:22.650 --> 01:10:25.358
We have nothing.
We've never seen a judge.


01:10:25.525 --> 01:10:26.567
We have nothing at all!


01:10:26.733 --> 01:10:27.567
They don't feed us!


01:10:27.692 --> 01:10:29.733
They won't even let us
go to the bathroom!


01:10:29.900 --> 01:10:33.317
The Red Cross dictates that
all prisoners must be treated fairly.


01:10:33.400 --> 01:10:35.608
-You want to use the bathroom?
-Of course I do.


01:10:35.692 --> 01:10:37.233
Take him to the bathroom immediately!


01:10:38.775 --> 01:10:39.858
What is your name?


01:10:40.025 --> 01:10:41.650
State your name.


01:10:46.108 --> 01:10:48.108
Eleuterio Fernández Huidobro.


01:10:48.567 --> 01:10:50.025
Dismissed.


01:10:50.442 --> 01:10:52.358
I said dismissed.


01:11:08.858 --> 01:11:10.192
State your name.


01:11:10.775 --> 01:11:11.817
Mauricio Rosencof.


01:11:12.858 --> 01:11:14.400
Dismissed.


01:11:18.525 --> 01:11:19.400
What is your name?


01:11:20.567 --> 01:11:21.775
José Alberto Mujica.


01:11:21.900 --> 01:11:23.567
Dismissed.


01:12:05.192 --> 01:12:07.858
Attention. Ten-hut!


01:12:15.942 --> 01:12:17.817
Take off his hood and get out.


01:12:22.067 --> 01:12:23.775
What the fuck is that?


01:12:24.358 --> 01:12:27.233
They made me come from Montevideo
for that crap so talk fast.


01:12:27.317 --> 01:12:29.983
Are you taking up arms again?


01:12:30.108 --> 01:12:32.983
What bullshit is that?
Contact with the outside?


01:12:33.108 --> 01:12:34.400
What for and who?


01:12:38.108 --> 01:12:40.692
What is the point of all this?
Go ahead.


01:12:41.817 --> 01:12:43.900
I remember how to make you talk.


01:12:43.983 --> 01:12:46.692
I'm being nice to you
so don't treat me like a fool.


01:12:46.858 --> 01:12:48.400
Did you make this?


01:12:48.858 --> 01:12:50.067
Give me the code.


01:12:50.192 --> 01:12:53.108
The message, damn it!
Give me the message right now!


01:12:55.358 --> 01:12:57.942
It's not a message,
it's a martingale.


01:12:58.525 --> 01:13:01.900
A system of chances to play roulette.


01:13:08.692 --> 01:13:10.483
Are you fucking with me?


01:13:11.108 --> 01:13:12.192
May I?


01:13:13.942 --> 01:13:16.650
A is the initial bet.


01:13:17.233 --> 01:13:19.608
B is the chance of losing.


01:13:20.025 --> 01:13:22.233
And N is the number of tries


01:13:22.317 --> 01:13:24.358
between the maximum and minimum bet.


01:13:24.525 --> 01:13:26.942
Let's suppose
your maximum bet is 1,000


01:13:27.275 --> 01:13:29.108
and the minimum is 10.


01:13:29.275 --> 01:13:30.900
You have to always play


01:13:30.983 --> 01:13:33.108
two chips at a time either red or black.


01:13:33.150 --> 01:13:36.733
That way the chances of winning
are higher. It's 50.5 %.


01:13:36.900 --> 01:13:40.150
So A=7, P=5


01:13:40.358 --> 01:13:43.067
and N=0,53.


01:13:43.275 --> 01:13:46.525
That gives you a chance
at winning of 20, 40,


01:13:46.650 --> 01:13:49.108
60, 80, 120, 360,


01:13:49.150 --> 01:13:50.733
460...


01:13:56.567 --> 01:13:58.192
You guys never change.


01:14:02.900 --> 01:14:05.983
Do you really think you'll beat
a whole system?


01:14:07.067 --> 01:14:10.483
It's too bad I didn't kill you
when I had the chance.


01:14:13.858 --> 01:14:16.817
Neither of us will ever forget that day.


01:14:20.275 --> 01:14:24.442
APRIL 14TH, 1972


01:14:28.983 --> 01:14:30.400
-Hi, how are you?
-Hi.


01:14:33.942 --> 01:14:35.733
Mom, I forgot my pencil case.


01:14:35.858 --> 01:14:36.858
Oh, darling.


01:14:37.233 --> 01:14:40.900
Don't worry, go inside and I'll go home
and bring it to you.


01:14:41.358 --> 01:14:42.233
Have fun.


01:14:42.317 --> 01:14:43.358
Bye.


01:14:57.692 --> 01:15:02.650
<i>Today, April 14th, 1972,</i>
<i>we leave behind Uruguay's</i>


01:15:02.817 --> 01:15:05.192
<i>bloodiest day in the 20th century.</i>


01:15:05.358 --> 01:15:08.317
<i>MLN Tupamaro commandos</i>
<i>have taken action</i>


01:15:08.400 --> 01:15:10.858
<i>against men they identified</i>
<i>as members of the Death Squad.</i>


01:15:10.983 --> 01:15:14.275
<i>In only hours, deputy commissioner</i>
<i>of the Interior</i>


01:15:14.483 --> 01:15:16.900
<i>Armando Acosta has died</i>


01:15:17.067 --> 01:15:19.983
<i>as well as deputy commissioner</i>
<i>Delega, Officer Leites,</i>


01:15:20.108 --> 01:15:21.233
<i>navy captain...</i>


01:15:21.442 --> 01:15:23.400
This is a declaration of war.


01:15:23.567 --> 01:15:27.650
<i>...deputy commissioner Reyes.</i>
<i>At ten this morning...</i>


01:15:27.817 --> 01:15:29.025
Turn it off.


01:15:29.650 --> 01:15:30.442
What?


01:15:30.567 --> 01:15:31.567
Turn off the radio.


01:15:38.358 --> 01:15:39.567
I don't hear anything.


01:15:40.650 --> 01:15:42.025
Exactly.


01:15:42.858 --> 01:15:44.358
Something's wrong.


01:17:37.442 --> 01:17:38.733
Move in!


01:18:13.567 --> 01:18:14.983
Answer it.


01:18:24.567 --> 01:18:25.900
They're down too.


01:18:30.733 --> 01:18:31.942
Move out.


01:18:35.567 --> 01:18:37.025
Tell me your name.


01:18:40.025 --> 01:18:41.192
What's your name?


01:18:42.900 --> 01:18:45.650
Luis Martirena.


01:18:45.817 --> 01:18:46.983
Luis Martirena.


01:18:47.233 --> 01:18:49.567
Good. So you're alive.


01:18:53.567 --> 01:18:56.233
<i>At 2 P.M. at Amazonas Street...</i>


01:18:56.442 --> 01:18:57.608
What do we do?


01:18:57.775 --> 01:19:00.108
<i>...near Aconcagua,</i>
<i>in the Malvín neighborhood,</i>


01:19:00.275 --> 01:19:02.983
<i>shots were fired between authorities</i>
<i>and Tupamaro guerrillas.</i>


01:19:03.108 --> 01:19:07.900
<i>Two guerrillas were killed.</i>
<i>Authorities continue to search...</i>


01:19:08.025 --> 01:19:09.442
Did you hear that?


01:19:10.108 --> 01:19:11.525
There were four of them.


01:19:12.192 --> 01:19:13.942
Only two dead.


01:19:14.025 --> 01:19:17.483
<i>...different clashes</i>
<i>and the city of Montevideo...</i>


01:19:27.483 --> 01:19:28.733
They're alive.


01:19:28.858 --> 01:19:30.942
Call Marcos and Cabrera.


01:19:31.108 --> 01:19:32.817
We have to prepare a rescue team.


01:22:03.858 --> 01:22:06.192
Shout that there are two of us.


01:22:06.400 --> 01:22:07.608
Shout my ass.


01:22:08.817 --> 01:22:11.483
I'm not leaving here alive.


01:22:16.400 --> 01:22:17.358
What's going on?


01:22:18.108 --> 01:22:19.275
Lower your weapon.


01:22:19.483 --> 01:22:21.025
There are two of us!


01:22:21.150 --> 01:22:22.567
We surrender!


01:22:24.400 --> 01:22:26.108
We surrender!


01:22:30.108 --> 01:22:32.150
<i>The world is full of idealists.</i>


01:22:32.983 --> 01:22:36.025
<i>Hell is full of good intentions.</i>


01:22:36.317 --> 01:22:38.108
This is your hell.


01:22:38.608 --> 01:22:41.733
I take responsibility for my mistakes
and the consequences.


01:22:41.817 --> 01:22:45.150
No, you take responsibility
for neither.


01:22:45.233 --> 01:22:47.358
We forced you to take responsibility.


01:22:48.275 --> 01:22:49.608
Your defeat


01:22:49.733 --> 01:22:50.942
forces you to.


01:22:51.108 --> 01:22:53.108
I did what I did because I believed in it.


01:22:53.150 --> 01:22:56.025
<i>I'm responsible and I accept</i>
<i>my punishment.</i>


01:22:56.108 --> 01:22:57.442
<i>Not you or anyone else</i>


01:22:57.525 --> 01:22:59.275
will take me for defeated.


01:23:01.150 --> 01:23:03.358
So you're not defeated?


01:23:05.608 --> 01:23:10.400
It's not the years that passed,
but think about the years that await you.


01:23:10.608 --> 01:23:12.733
You'll never get out of here.


01:23:13.358 --> 01:23:15.025
I might die here,


01:23:16.108 --> 01:23:17.525
but when that happens,


01:23:19.483 --> 01:23:21.400
I know the weight of my burden.


01:23:21.942 --> 01:23:23.150
But you,


01:23:23.358 --> 01:23:25.900
do you know how much yours weighs?


01:23:27.108 --> 01:23:29.025
<i>I belonged to this world.</i>


01:23:30.317 --> 01:23:32.400
<i>Now everything is foreign to me.</i>
<i>The sunrise,</i>


01:23:32.525 --> 01:23:34.025
the sound of the birds...


01:23:35.525 --> 01:23:37.358
You're foreign to me.


01:24:23.858 --> 01:24:26.692
-Hello, son. How are you?
-Fine, Mom.


01:24:27.775 --> 01:24:29.733
Grandpa sends his love.


01:24:30.692 --> 01:24:33.108
Always reminding me
to bring you things.


01:24:34.650 --> 01:24:37.150
He says: "Don't forget to bring
<i>dulce de leche</i>


01:24:37.650 --> 01:24:39.775
and two kilos of<i> mate."</i>


01:24:40.275 --> 01:24:42.608
I know they're going
to take away some things,


01:24:42.775 --> 01:24:45.067
but something might be left.


01:24:45.400 --> 01:24:47.525
-Is that okay?
-Mom.


01:24:48.108 --> 01:24:49.900
You have to stop coming.


01:24:50.108 --> 01:24:51.275
What?


01:24:51.483 --> 01:24:52.400
Why?


01:24:52.942 --> 01:24:55.775
It's too long to explain, Mom.


01:24:55.900 --> 01:25:00.733
They're persecuting us,
it's like an attack


01:25:00.858 --> 01:25:03.400
with sound, ultrasound, I don't know.


01:25:03.567 --> 01:25:06.275
My ear is hot. Listen, Mom.


01:25:06.442 --> 01:25:09.442
They put a voice or an antenna
inside me.


01:25:09.567 --> 01:25:11.400
I can't stop thinking.


01:25:11.567 --> 01:25:15.025
Whenever I stop, they attack me again.


01:25:15.150 --> 01:25:17.692
They haven't gotten into
my thoughts for a while...


01:25:17.858 --> 01:25:19.067
Stop.


01:25:20.067 --> 01:25:22.733
What matters is I have it
all under control.


01:25:22.900 --> 01:25:25.733
-But you have to not come for a while.
-Son...


01:25:25.900 --> 01:25:28.733
What do you think they are?


01:25:28.858 --> 01:25:32.108
-Nuns in a charity?
-Shut up!


01:25:32.275 --> 01:25:33.192
Shut up!


01:25:35.900 --> 01:25:37.025
Listen to me!


01:25:37.358 --> 01:25:40.233
I'm the one you have
to listen to. I'm your mother.


01:25:40.692 --> 01:25:42.358
They want to drive you crazy.


01:25:42.442 --> 01:25:44.483
You can't let them.


01:25:44.983 --> 01:25:46.525
Do you understand?


01:25:46.817 --> 01:25:47.942
Mom...


01:25:48.108 --> 01:25:49.442
Mom my ass!


01:25:49.608 --> 01:25:51.067
Mom my ass!


01:25:51.192 --> 01:25:52.150
Listen to me.


01:25:52.233 --> 01:25:55.900
Listen to what I have to say.
You have to resist.


01:25:55.983 --> 01:25:57.442
Resist


01:25:57.608 --> 01:25:59.775
any way you can,
no matter what happens.


01:25:59.858 --> 01:26:03.150
Resist and don't let them kill you.


01:26:04.650 --> 01:26:06.150
I don't know how.


01:26:08.692 --> 01:26:10.067
Yes, you do.


01:26:11.442 --> 01:26:13.108
The only defeated


01:26:13.275 --> 01:26:15.442
are the ones who stop fighting.


01:26:17.233 --> 01:26:20.525
You'll get through this and move on.


01:26:21.858 --> 01:26:23.275
And nobody...


01:26:24.483 --> 01:26:27.358
Nobody will take
what you have inside.


01:26:57.025 --> 01:26:58.817
Heat the water at least.


01:27:34.900 --> 01:27:39.400
168 years ago today,


01:27:39.775 --> 01:27:43.108
by the hand of our leader,


01:27:43.567 --> 01:27:48.150
our magnificent commander,
one of a kind on Earth,


01:27:48.650 --> 01:27:50.983
when the people gathered


01:27:51.067 --> 01:27:53.108
to seek their freedom...


01:27:53.150 --> 01:27:55.483
I want my<i> mate</i> and my potty!


01:27:55.567 --> 01:27:57.608
I need to take a shit!


01:27:57.900 --> 01:27:59.483
I want my<i> mate</i> and my potty!


01:27:59.733 --> 01:28:02.775
Fucking son of a bitch!


01:28:03.025 --> 01:28:04.942
I want my potty!


01:28:05.192 --> 01:28:08.483
Remembering the historic process...


01:28:08.567 --> 01:28:10.775
Give me back my potty!


01:28:10.942 --> 01:28:12.108
And my<i> mate!</i>


01:28:12.525 --> 01:28:14.733
You're going to smell
what comes out of my ass!


01:28:14.900 --> 01:28:17.692
Your Sunday clothes will stink!


01:28:18.483 --> 01:28:20.150
I want my potty!


01:28:20.233 --> 01:28:22.067
I need to take a shit!


01:28:22.192 --> 01:28:23.233
Filthy bastard!


01:28:23.442 --> 01:28:24.983
I want my potty!


01:28:25.525 --> 01:28:28.317
Fucking son of a bitch!


01:28:28.650 --> 01:28:29.692
Be quiet.


01:28:30.192 --> 01:28:31.483
Come here, Sapito!


01:28:31.650 --> 01:28:32.567
Come here!


01:28:33.192 --> 01:28:35.400
Come here, Sapito!
Come here!


01:28:35.567 --> 01:28:38.108
Bring your bayonet,
just you and me.


01:28:38.233 --> 01:28:39.067
Come on, you and me.


01:28:41.025 --> 01:28:42.817
How do you know I'm Sapito?


01:28:43.275 --> 01:28:47.900
Want me to tell them you cheated
on your wife with that whore?


01:28:48.692 --> 01:28:51.358
Sapito cheated on his wife!
You hear me?


01:28:51.525 --> 01:28:53.233
Sapito has a lover!


01:28:53.442 --> 01:28:54.525
Son of a bitch!


01:28:54.775 --> 01:28:56.983
Do they know you got syphilis?


01:28:57.108 --> 01:28:59.650
-Because you fucked her...
-Where did you hear that?


01:28:59.733 --> 01:29:02.400
-Sapito has syphilis!
-Shut the fuck up!


01:29:02.567 --> 01:29:03.858
What the fuck do you want?


01:29:04.942 --> 01:29:06.817
My potty and my<i> mate.</i>


01:29:07.108 --> 01:29:08.900
That my mom brought.


01:29:10.400 --> 01:29:13.067
And bring some hot water
for the<i> mate.</i>


01:29:13.192 --> 01:29:15.067
I don't like the water warm.


01:29:15.275 --> 01:29:18.358
-Maybe he has a periscope.
-He definitely has a periscope.


01:29:21.358 --> 01:29:23.608
Do you even know what a periscope is?


01:29:24.900 --> 01:29:27.025
What are you talking about, moron?


01:29:28.150 --> 01:29:31.025
We need to keep an eye
on this filthy bastard.


01:29:31.400 --> 01:29:33.442
We'll have to call our superiors.


01:30:05.067 --> 01:30:06.983
<i>So, tell me.</i>


01:30:07.358 --> 01:30:11.858
You have a device, an antenna.
Who put it there?


01:30:12.108 --> 01:30:13.983
How should I know, doctor?


01:30:14.275 --> 01:30:15.900
I imagine the army,


01:30:15.983 --> 01:30:17.358
the CIA, I don't know.


01:30:17.525 --> 01:30:18.775
What does it say?


01:30:19.400 --> 01:30:20.900
It's a voice here.


01:30:21.025 --> 01:30:22.483
It insults me.


01:30:22.608 --> 01:30:25.608
It wants to control my thoughts,
get information out of me...


01:30:25.733 --> 01:30:28.858
It sends me an electric pulse,


01:30:28.942 --> 01:30:34.108
it sends me heat here, in my ear...
A fire here burns me.


01:30:35.233 --> 01:30:37.275
Have you had any


01:30:37.650 --> 01:30:39.608
episodes of anxiety, distress,


01:30:39.775 --> 01:30:40.983
fear?


01:30:42.192 --> 01:30:44.233
Any stressful situations?


01:30:46.983 --> 01:30:49.233
Do you sleep well? Do you rest?


01:30:49.442 --> 01:30:51.275
Yeah, he rests.


01:30:52.900 --> 01:30:54.858
Do you eat right?


01:30:55.942 --> 01:30:57.025
More or less.


01:30:57.150 --> 01:30:58.983
He eats everything we give him.


01:31:01.150 --> 01:31:03.567
Soldier, I need to work calmly.


01:31:03.733 --> 01:31:07.650
So bring some water, please.


01:31:08.525 --> 01:31:09.900
Go and get some water.


01:31:28.067 --> 01:31:32.983
Mujica, all of these symptoms you have
appear to be...


01:31:34.025 --> 01:31:36.192
a delusional psychosis.


01:31:37.025 --> 01:31:40.108
We still don't know if it's chronic,
if it's acute...


01:31:40.275 --> 01:31:42.358
We need more time to evaluate.


01:31:42.525 --> 01:31:44.942
But that's what's making you feel...


01:31:46.233 --> 01:31:49.483
confused and unable to reason.


01:31:49.650 --> 01:31:52.692
Part of your disorder has to do with
not being able to rest.


01:31:52.858 --> 01:31:56.108
Right now what will help you
the most is sleeping at night.


01:31:56.233 --> 01:31:58.192
Take some pills and sleep.


01:31:58.900 --> 01:32:00.608
That's what I'm going to prescribe.


01:32:02.817 --> 01:32:05.150
I don't need to sleep, doctor.


01:32:07.233 --> 01:32:10.942
-You don't? And what do you need?
-To stop thinking.


01:32:13.233 --> 01:32:15.733
What will help you


01:32:15.858 --> 01:32:17.817
to stop thinking?


01:32:18.108 --> 01:32:19.442
To use my hands,


01:32:20.108 --> 01:32:21.858
to organize my head.


01:32:22.775 --> 01:32:23.983
To write,


01:32:24.608 --> 01:32:25.733
read...


01:32:27.400 --> 01:32:29.233
To read and write.


01:32:29.775 --> 01:32:33.108
I'll have them send you something
to read and paper


01:32:33.150 --> 01:32:34.442
and a pen to write with.


01:32:34.858 --> 01:32:36.858
I haven't read in 7 years.


01:32:37.025 --> 01:32:40.358
You have to cling to anything
you can right now, Mujica.


01:32:41.108 --> 01:32:43.858
Anything that you have at hand.


01:32:44.692 --> 01:32:46.900
Are you religious?
Do you believe in God?


01:32:47.442 --> 01:32:48.942
What god would do this?


01:32:50.525 --> 01:32:52.817
The only one we've got,
unfortunately.


01:32:52.983 --> 01:32:57.775
If the god you believe in remains silent,


01:32:58.108 --> 01:33:00.150
and you say I'm crazy,


01:33:02.358 --> 01:33:03.983
what do I cling to?


01:33:05.775 --> 01:33:09.608
You're the first
woman I've seen in years.


01:33:10.817 --> 01:33:14.983
I haven't seen the stars
or light for years.


01:33:16.233 --> 01:33:19.525
And you talk to me
about reason, what reason?


01:33:20.858 --> 01:33:23.567
Look, I'm going to tell you a story.


01:33:24.442 --> 01:33:26.358
When I was 15 years old,


01:33:27.025 --> 01:33:29.233
I saw my mother die of cancer.


01:33:30.108 --> 01:33:35.442
And that was when I decided
to become a doctor.


01:33:35.525 --> 01:33:37.733
So I studied and got my degree.


01:33:37.942 --> 01:33:42.733
I saw hundreds, thousands of patients
those 20 years.


01:33:42.900 --> 01:33:46.817
But one day I got up
and didn't want to come to work.


01:33:46.983 --> 01:33:49.775
I couldn't leave the house,
I couldn't get up.


01:33:49.858 --> 01:33:51.275
I didn't want to talk to anyone.


01:33:52.525 --> 01:33:55.233
And I thought and I thought
and I thought.


01:33:57.192 --> 01:33:58.400
Like you.


01:33:59.108 --> 01:34:01.108
Until I realized


01:34:02.858 --> 01:34:04.733
that no matter what I did,


01:34:05.358 --> 01:34:06.567
my mother


01:34:08.525 --> 01:34:09.900
would still be dead.


01:34:13.233 --> 01:34:16.275
That's when I got up
and went back to work.


01:34:17.150 --> 01:34:19.900
And here I am, doing what I can,


01:34:20.483 --> 01:34:23.400
asking you to do what you can.


01:34:23.983 --> 01:34:26.692
To cling to anything you can.


01:34:27.108 --> 01:34:28.692
Ma'am.


01:34:33.192 --> 01:34:34.942
All set? Can I take him?


01:34:35.108 --> 01:34:36.483
Yes.


01:34:44.150 --> 01:34:45.192
Soldier.


01:34:45.400 --> 01:34:47.692
I need him to sign the diagnosis.


01:34:51.108 --> 01:34:52.025
All right.


01:34:55.108 --> 01:34:58.400
I'll get you something
to read and write.


01:34:59.233 --> 01:35:00.483
Be strong.


01:35:00.983 --> 01:35:02.150
Survive.


01:35:02.358 --> 01:35:03.900
It's almost over.


01:35:06.025 --> 01:35:07.233
Come on, Mujica.


01:35:08.817 --> 01:35:11.525
<i>Yes, for my country.</i>


01:35:12.775 --> 01:35:15.733
<i>Yes, for Uruguay.</i>


01:35:16.108 --> 01:35:19.483
<i>Yes, for progress</i>


01:35:19.817 --> 01:35:22.775
<i>and yes, for peace.</i>


01:35:23.275 --> 01:35:27.442
2757 DAYS


01:35:27.608 --> 01:35:30.608
<i>...we're going to vote.</i>


01:35:30.858 --> 01:35:34.442
<i>Yes, for greatness.</i>


01:35:34.608 --> 01:35:37.900
<i>Yes, for Uruguay.</i>


01:35:40.400 --> 01:35:42.025
<i>Voting booths have closed</i>


01:35:42.150 --> 01:35:45.525
<i>with 20 % of the votes counted.</i>


01:35:45.692 --> 01:35:47.733
<i>Here are the results:</i>


01:35:47.900 --> 01:35:52.525
<i>39 % "no," 61 % "yes."</i>


01:35:53.108 --> 01:35:54.442
<i>In Maldonado...</i>


01:35:55.025 --> 01:36:00.400
<i>Are we "yes" or "no"?</i>


01:36:03.858 --> 01:36:06.900
<i>I don't know.</i>


01:36:11.692 --> 01:36:13.608
Take this, little shit!


01:36:21.525 --> 01:36:24.025
It's a disgrace, a disgraceful defeat.


01:36:24.150 --> 01:36:26.942
-What will happen?
-Who knows?


01:36:28.942 --> 01:36:32.692
<i>Against all predictions,</i>
<i>with 80 % of all votes counted,</i>


01:36:32.858 --> 01:36:36.067
<i>the surprising defeat of the "yes" vote</i>
<i>has been confirmed.</i>


01:36:36.192 --> 01:36:38.692
<i>The Uruguayan people</i>
<i>said a resounding "no"</i>


01:36:38.858 --> 01:36:42.108
<i>to the constitutional project</i>
<i>proposed by the government,</i>


01:36:42.275 --> 01:36:45.192
<i>which is now headed</i>
<i>for a period of negotiation</i>


01:36:45.400 --> 01:36:47.400
<i>towards a possible democracy.</i>


01:38:20.233 --> 01:38:24.942
3053 DAYS


01:38:28.150 --> 01:38:32.483
3518 DAYS


01:38:49.025 --> 01:38:53.567
3883 DAYS


01:39:12.608 --> 01:39:14.525
Doctor, I want a detailed report


01:39:14.692 --> 01:39:16.483
on the condition of this guy
they've sent us.


01:39:16.650 --> 01:39:18.608
Get out.
Everybody out!


01:39:23.983 --> 01:39:25.567
Rosencof.


01:39:26.025 --> 01:39:27.858
You're back here again?


01:39:28.650 --> 01:39:29.733
Sergeant.


01:39:31.108 --> 01:39:32.733
And your girlfriend?


01:39:40.567 --> 01:39:41.858
Congratulations.


01:39:42.025 --> 01:39:42.900
Thank you.


01:39:44.025 --> 01:39:45.192
But she reproaches me:


01:39:46.108 --> 01:39:49.650
"When we were going out
you used to write me,


01:39:49.817 --> 01:39:50.942
but not anymore."


01:39:54.400 --> 01:39:56.942
Tell me, what can I do for you?


01:41:24.942 --> 01:41:25.692
Pepe.


01:41:26.400 --> 01:41:27.942
Ruso. Ruso.


01:41:28.192 --> 01:41:29.442
We're alone.


01:41:30.442 --> 01:41:31.900
We're alone.


01:41:39.983 --> 01:41:41.150
Do you see anything?


01:41:41.442 --> 01:41:42.650
We're heading south.


01:41:42.858 --> 01:41:43.650
What do you see?


01:42:03.525 --> 01:42:07.275
3989 DAYS


01:43:40.817 --> 01:43:41.942
It's Ñato!


01:43:46.025 --> 01:43:47.525
Let's go, Ñato!


01:43:51.983 --> 01:43:54.525
Let's go, Ñato!


01:44:26.192 --> 01:44:27.775
Let's go, Ñato!


01:45:10.192 --> 01:45:11.567
<i>Who's here, Tato?</i>


01:45:11.733 --> 01:45:13.025
<i>What for, Ñato?</i>


01:45:13.900 --> 01:45:15.400
Is Berreta here?


01:45:15.858 --> 01:45:18.858
Yeah, yeah.
He's on the fourth floor.


01:45:19.442 --> 01:45:20.608
And Arriosa?


01:45:21.608 --> 01:45:23.692
No, Ñato. Arriosa isn't.


01:45:24.733 --> 01:45:27.483
And Sanzo? Is Sanzo here?


01:45:30.192 --> 01:45:34.817
No, Ñato. Sanzo went down too.
We never heard anything again.


01:45:40.733 --> 01:45:41.817
And Varela?


01:45:42.983 --> 01:45:47.192
<i>He disappeared.</i>
<i>They took him one day. No idea.</i>


01:45:52.900 --> 01:45:55.317
<i>And Medina? Is Medina here?</i>


01:45:59.650 --> 01:46:00.942
<i>And Lucho?</i>


01:46:03.025 --> 01:46:04.358
<i>Is Lucho here?</i>


01:46:50.858 --> 01:46:54.608
4323 DAYS


01:46:55.858 --> 01:46:57.608
Mujica, get ready.


01:47:20.108 --> 01:47:21.108
Sign here.


01:47:23.692 --> 01:47:26.692
It confirms that
you were treated correctly.


01:47:38.400 --> 01:47:40.233
This doesn't end here.


01:47:40.442 --> 01:47:41.608
Don't get your hopes up.


01:47:41.775 --> 01:47:45.192
When you're out, we'll find you
and nobody will save you there.


01:47:45.400 --> 01:47:46.525
You hear me?


01:47:46.650 --> 01:47:48.942
There are no political
responsibilities out there.


01:47:49.108 --> 01:47:50.858
I wish you the best.


01:48:25.025 --> 01:48:25.900
Ñato!


01:48:27.650 --> 01:48:29.233
We're leaving.


01:48:30.733 --> 01:48:32.067
Come on, Ñato, we're leaving!


01:48:45.025 --> 01:48:46.192
What are you doing?


01:48:46.983 --> 01:48:48.400
Why are you still washing?


01:48:51.233 --> 01:48:52.900
For the next ones.


01:48:54.692 --> 01:48:56.900
If I were you, I'd get moving.


01:50:28.608 --> 01:50:29.817
Dad!


01:50:30.108 --> 01:50:31.733
Jorge Benitez' family!


01:50:33.483 --> 01:50:35.733
-Grandpa!
-Dad!


01:50:46.817 --> 01:50:48.525
WE DIDN'T FORGET YOU


01:50:52.150 --> 01:50:55.567
Carlos González' family!


01:50:57.275 --> 01:50:59.567
Roberto Hipólito's family!


01:51:00.817 --> 01:51:03.233
Washington González' family!


01:51:06.900 --> 01:51:08.983
Marcelo Jiménez' family!


01:51:22.900 --> 01:51:24.525
Is that Daddy?


01:51:24.692 --> 01:51:25.900
I don't know, wait and see.


01:51:30.775 --> 01:51:32.567
Daddy!


01:52:45.942 --> 01:52:46.942
Graciela!


01:52:47.525 --> 01:52:48.358
Graciela!


01:52:51.817 --> 01:52:53.275
Ñato! Ñato!


01:53:02.692 --> 01:53:04.608
José Mujica Cordano.


01:53:04.775 --> 01:53:07.483
José Mujica Cordano's family!


01:53:39.983 --> 01:53:43.608
After 12 years of solitary confinement,
upon the return to democracy,


01:53:43.775 --> 01:53:46.067
the prisoners were freed.


01:53:59.358 --> 01:54:02.358
<i>The people united</i>
<i>will never be defeated!</i>


01:54:08.358 --> 01:54:12.650
Eleuterio Fernández Huidobro
was a senator and Defense Minister.


01:54:12.817 --> 01:54:16.983
He died on August 5th, 2016.


01:54:20.608 --> 01:54:25.192
Mauricio Rosencof lives in Montevideo.
He's a poet, novelist and playwright.


01:54:25.275 --> 01:54:29.317
He was Cultural Director
for the city of Montevideo.


01:54:36.733 --> 01:54:41.442
José Mujica was
a congressman and senator.


01:54:42.108 --> 01:54:48.108
In 2010, at age 75, he was elected
President of Uruguay.


01:55:00.358 --> 01:55:03.817
<i>Where is your bird?</i>


01:55:04.900 --> 01:55:07.192
<i>Where?</i>


01:55:09.067 --> 01:55:14.400
<i>Tell me where your bird is.</i>


01:55:19.733 --> 01:55:24.400
<i>My bird is a dream</i>


01:55:25.942 --> 01:55:28.067
<i>and it flew away.</i>


01:55:30.858 --> 01:55:34.858
<i>My bird is a dream...</i>


01:55:37.650 --> 01:55:41.692
<i>and it flew away.</i>


01:55:42.567 --> 01:55:44.817
<i>Ask me</i>


01:55:45.525 --> 01:55:47.192
<i>if it will come back.</i>


01:55:47.733 --> 01:55:48.900
<i>Come back,</i>


01:55:49.442 --> 01:55:50.900
<i>come back,</i>


01:55:51.608 --> 01:55:54.108
<i>come back...</i>


01:55:57.692 --> 01:56:01.275
<i>and never leaves.</i>


01:56:02.483 --> 01:56:05.817
<i>And it flies and stays.</i>


01:56:07.025 --> 01:56:10.900
<i>It flies and stays.</i>


01:56:12.150 --> 01:56:15.442
<i>It's all a dream.</i>


01:56:16.608 --> 01:56:19.692
<i>A dream.</i>


01:56:21.108 --> 01:56:23.858
<i>It's all a dream.</i>

